{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["Now Moshe was tending the flock, etc. — And the Holy One, blessed be He, appeared to him and commanded him to return to Egypt, but Moshe did not want to, for he was afraid, until the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״כי מתו כל האנשים המבקשים את נפשך״ — this is Pharaoh, who died. Therefore Scripture says: וימת מלך מצרים, to testify to what the Holy One, blessed be He, said: ״כי מתו כל האנשים״, etc. — just as (Scripture states) ״וחם הוא אבי כנען״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The closing comparison 'כמו: וחם הוא אבי כנען' cites Genesis 9:18 as another example of Scripture providing a clarifying parenthetical aside; rendered here without a full address since Rashbam himself gives none."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:14.920078018Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}